 "trap_class": "symmetry mate contacts",
 "intent": "Count the atom pairs closer than 4.0 Angstrom between chain A and chain B of peptide_pair.pdb, the two peptides as they are placed in the model file, to see whether the two peptides touch each other, and write the count to contacts.txt.",
 "silent_error": "gemmi.NeighborSearch(model, st.cell, ...) is symmetry aware: with a CRYST1 cell and space group (P 21 21 21 here) ContactSearch also reports contacts to symmetry copies (Result.image_idx != 0). The loop filters only on chain names, so contacts between chain A and a symmetry mate of chain B are counted as A-B contacts. The script prints 24 pairs although the closest A-B atoms in the coordinates of the file are 32.7 A apart (the true count is 0). gemmi documents the symmetry-aware search and the image_idx field of ContactSearch results; nothing is printed to say that images were used. Exit status 0, empty stderr.",
 "files": {
  "contacts.py": "import sys\nimport gemmi\n\nst = gemmi.read_structure(sys.argv[1])\nmodel = st[0]\nns = gemmi.NeighborSearch(model, st.cell, 5).populate()\ncs = gemmi.ContactSearch(4.0)\ncs.ignore = gemmi.ContactSearch.Ignore.SameChain\ncount = 0\nfor r in cs.find_contacts(ns):\n    if {r.partner1.chain.name, r.partner2.chain.name} == {'A', 'B'}:\n        count += 1\nprint('A-B atom pairs within 4.0 A:', count)\n",
  "contacts_v2.py": "import sys\nimport gemmi\n\nst = gemmi.read_structure(sys.argv[1])\nmodel = st[0]\nns = gemmi.NeighborSearch(model, st.cell, 5).populate()\ncs = gemmi.ContactSearch(4.0)\ncs.ignore = gemmi.ContactSearch.Ignore.SameChain\ncount = 0\nfor r in cs.find_contacts(ns):\n    if r.image_idx != 0:\n        continue\n    if {r.partner1.chain.name, r.partner2.chain.name} == {'A', 'B'}:\n        count += 1\nprint('A-B atom pairs within 4.0 A:', count)\n",
